  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "contrast_t",
   "x": 66,
   "y": 386,
   "width": 488,
   "height": 118,
   "text": "vs an LLM\n\nAn LLM emits `true`/`false` (or a\nmade-up 'confident' bool) — you can't tell a\n0.51 call from a 0.99 one. Noul returns the\nPROBABILITY; you own the threshold, and it's\ncalibrated.",
   "originalText": "vs an LLM\n\nAn LLM emits `true`/`false` (or a\nmade-up 'confident' bool) — you can't tell a\n0.51 call from a 0.99 one. Noul returns the\nPROBABILITY; you own the threshold, and it's\ncalibrated.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
